# Exactly the artifact llama-server's own --fim-qwen-7b-default resolves to, so
# the prefix/suffix/middle special tokens the /infill endpoint needs are known
# present rather than assumed. Served plain: /infill reads FIM tokens from the
# GGUF, no chat template involved.
SIDECAR_PORT=8084
SIDECAR_ALIAS=qwen25-coder-7b-fim
SIDECAR_MODEL=/home/typhoon/git/frankenstein-llm/models/fim/qwen2.5-coder-7b-q8_0.gguf
SIDECAR_DEVICE=ROCm0,ROCm1,ROCm2
SIDECAR_NGL=all
SIDECAR_CTX=32768
SIDECAR_BATCH=1024
SIDECAR_UBATCH=512
# Placement: one card. 3,6,2 was the pre-2026-09-06 catalog default and gave the
# throttling V620 the majority of the layers of a model that fits on a single
# 6900 XT. llama-models.ini stopped using it in f2576ac; this file was not
# updated with it. Layer split is pipelined, so every token crossed two extra
# devices for no capacity reason. Measured on kernel 7.2.3-273-tkg-eevdf-llvm,
# pp512/tg128, r=3, native llama-bench: 42.13 -> 58.17 tok/s decode (+38.1%),
# 2074.37 -> 2467.06 tok/s prefill (+18.9%). Infill generates, so both apply.
SIDECAR_EXTRA_ARGS=--cache-type-k q8_0 --cache-type-v q8_0 --flash-attn on --tensor-split 1,0,0
